        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 25 at 3:09PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "An Arctic cold front is expected to move southeast from the\nChukchi Sea Saturday night into Sunday. Starting off, most of the\nprecipitation will be rain and then transition to snow early\nSunday morning. During this transition, there is a slight chance\nfor sleet and/or freezing drizzle to fall along the eastern Arctic\nCoast. Snow accumulations of 2-6\" is possible in the Brooks Range\nwith less than an inch expected for most of the Eastern Arctic\nCoast. Periods of freezing drizzle are possible as t",
